===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|postpositive|used only with indefinite or interrogative pronouns}} [[other|Other]]; in [[addition]] to previously mentioned items.
#: {{ux|en|The instructor is busy. Can anyone '''else''' help me?}}
#: {{ux|en|Whatever '''else''' she may be, she is not a surgeon.}}
#: {{ux|en|When all '''else''' fails, read the instructions.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Tempest|I|ii|text={{smallcaps|Prospero}}:<br>Thou hast done well, fine Ariel. Follow me;<br>[[hark|Hark]] what thou '''else''' shalt do me.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=Keith T. Krawczynski|title=Daily Life in the Colonial City|passage=As with most '''else''' in society, early Americans believed that health and healing were in God's hand.}}

====Usage notes====
* This adjective usually follows an [[indefinite]] or [[interrogative]] pronoun, as in the examples above. In other cases, the adjective {{m|en|other}} is typically used.

